Rāma charges Vālin ignorant of dharma custom and counsel --- Rāma claims Bharata rules Ikṣvāku earth justly --- Rāma condemns Vālin lusting after Rumā as death-worthy --- Rāma cites alliance vow and Bharata command --- Rāma invokes Māndhātā precedent and hunter blamelessness --- Rāma warns kings walk as gods inviolable --- Vālin admits inferiority and begs forgiveness --- Vālin entrusts Aṅgada and Tārā to Rāma care --- Rāma consoles cleansed Vālin and wins apology